      The square metal grate in the concrete floor is the drain, and there is something gold glinting at the bottom of it — you can see it through the slots long before you can reach it. Select the <b>Lit blowtorch</b>, press <b>Use</b> and tap the grate: the metal burns through and the opening is clear, but it is still too narrow to put a hand in. Now select the <b>Hook</b>, press <b>Use</b> and tap the drain again. The hook goes down and comes back up with a small brass <b>Key</b>. Two items, two verbs, one hole — this is the only place in the DIY Shop where the game makes you use tools you built rather than tools you found.
