      Go back to the blue tool chest under the button panel — the one with the yellow hard hat sitting on top. The lower drawer is locked and the brass key fits it. Use the key on the drawer and it slides open on a rolled sheet of paper: pick it up and the label reads <b>Blueprint</b>. It looks like a blank roll at first, which is why the next step matters. Do not try to read it from the bag; the bag only shows you a rolled tube.
