      On the grey wall panel in the back room there is a keypad with twelve keys — digits 1 to 9, a zero, a backspace key marked with an x and a tick — and three display slots above them under a yellow padlock icon. Type <b>954</b> and press the tick. The slots fill as you press so you can check the entry before you commit, and the backspace clears one digit at a time rather than the whole code. Three digits, three slots, no padding and no leading zero.
